  "summary": "Recent preprints and papers define distinct adaptors, tethers and routes that remodel organelles under starvation, iron deficiency and osmotic stress.",
  "synthesis": "The items converge on stress-triggered remodeling of organelles through degradative and membrane-supply routes, mainly autophagy. Lipid and contact-site control appears in yeast, where Mdm1 balances phospholipid and neutral lipid metabolism to allow autophagosome completion, and in HeLa cells, where ATAD1 at mitochondria-ER contacts moves mislocalized Pex26 from mitochondria to the ER. Iron deficiency triggers pexophagy through a GABARAP-FLCN/FNIP1 interaction that activates TFEB and TFE3. Acinus-induced autophagy requires Rab32 and Lrrk kinase rather than mTor regulation, and RAB11-RAB30 drives endosomal remodeling through a phosphoinositide switch under starvation, shear and osmotic stress. What is new is the assignment of specific adaptors, tethers and signaling routes to each context, rather than a single shared mechanism.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-25"
}
